**A Missed Flight**
While Mary Wilson was at the airport, she asked the clerk to tell her whether her flight had been cancelled, but the clerk refused to do so.
The following hour, the passenger asked to use the public telephone.
When she was alone, she telephoned the airline office and asked for Mr Davis.
When the officer answered the phone, Miss Wilson said she was calling to ask about a certain passenger, a Miss Mary Wilson.
She asked if Miss Wilson’s flight had been cancelled and the officer told her that it had been.
She then asked when Miss Wilson would be able to take the next flight and the officer told her that she would have to wait another three hours.
Then Mr Davis asked the caller if she was a friend of the passenger.
‘No,’ the passenger answered, ‘I am Miss Mary Wilson.’